        "original_id": "8625fc7a-bb0e-5071-8d31-d91cde23e8a8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Coffee cherry tea, cascara sagrada tea\n- Plants: Rhamnus purshiana, Frangula purshiana, Rhamnus purshianus\n- Places: Western North America, southern British Columbia, central California, northwestern Montana\n- Concepts: Plant-based laxatives, common names, synonyms\n\nFacts:\n- Coffee cherry tea is different from cascara sagrada tea, which is a powerful plant-based laxative.\n- Rhamnus purshiana is also known as cascara buckthorn, cascara, bearberry, chittem, and chitticum.\n- Frangula purshiana and Rhamnus purshianus are synonyms for Rhamnus purshiana.\n- Rhamnus purshiana is a species of buckthorn native to western North America.\n- Rhamnus purshiana ranges from southern British Columbia south to central California and eastward to northwestern Montana.",
